# tools/a/aurora_file_placement_witness.rish -- the unit the capacity forced.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/a/aurora_file_placement_witness.rish
#
# Row 7 of `active-designing/20260910-060204_the-bounded-torus-moonshots.md` proposes a placement
# map as its first witness. Its second erratum found that every assignment of MODULES to nodes
# overflows a node at either grid the row names, and closed on one named step nobody had taken:
#
#   "name which FILES sit on which node rather than which modules, since the coarsening the first
#    erratum called the harder half is forced rather than optional"
#
# This witness takes that step and grades three things.
#
# WHERE THE UNIT STOPS FITTING. The file unit is not free of the constraint that forced it. Divide
# tracked Rye bytes by the node count and compare the largest single file: it fits at four nodes and
# at sixteen, and overflows at sixty-four. So the erratum's "one level down" has its own ceiling,
# one grid above the largest the row names.
#
# WHAT THE FINER GRAPH HOLDS. Resolving imports at file granularity through this tree's hand-filed
# symlinks gives a graph far larger than the room graph beside it -- and the share that matters is
# the one a room graph cannot see at all: an edge whose two files sit in ONE room. Those edges are
# free by construction under any module placement, because both endpoints land on one node.
#
# WHAT THE FORCED UNIT COSTS. Capacity forbids the module placement, so that free traffic becomes
# real hops. The scan prints both shares beside each other, and the gap between them is the price
# of the coarsening the row cannot have.
#
# WHAT THIS WITNESS DOES NOT REACH. Whether a torus board arrives, and whether these files are the
# unit a real Aurora would place. The import graph is STRUCTURE read as a lower bound on coupling,
# with the tolerance its sibling measured; a run-time weight would differ, and this tree holds none.

say "aurora-file-placement: Style Gauge, Meter -- the unit a capacity constraint leaves available."
say "aurora-file-placement: Lens TAME -- a baseline free to spread loses to any layout at all."

# --- The reading -------------------------------------------------------------
say "aurora-file-placement: reading the unit, the graph and the placement..."
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/a/aurora_file_placement_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "aurora-file-placement: the scan refused -- read its own keys"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=read" else "aurora-file-placement: the scan reached no verdict"

# invariant: the reading names the row it grades and the page whose named step it takes, so a key
# pasted out of context still says which sentence it is about.
assert scan.out contains "row=7" else "aurora-file-placement: the reading named no row"
assert scan.out contains "the-bounded-torus-moonshots.md" else "aurora-file-placement: the reading named no page"
assert scan.out contains "the-two-ways-a-proxy-drifts.md" else "aurora-file-placement: the reading named no answered step"

# --- The bounds --------------------------------------------------------------
# invariant: every collection this scan builds names its maximum, so a tree that grows past one is
# refused at the edge rather than read short in silence.
assert scan.out contains "max_files=" else "aurora-file-placement: the file bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "max_edges=" else "aurora-file-placement: the edge bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "max_grids=" else "aurora-file-placement: the grid bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "max_samples=" else "aurora-file-placement: the baseline bound is unnamed"
assert scan.out contains "cap_slack_pct=" else "aurora-file-placement: the capacity slack is unnamed"

# --- READING 1 -- where the unit stops fitting -------------------------------
# invariant: the population was opened at all. A tree of no Rye sources would let every later key
# read clean while measuring nothing, so the scan answers `empty` there rather than `read`.
assert scan.out contains "rye_files=" else "aurora-file-placement: no file census was taken"
assert scan.out contains "rye_bytes_total=" else "aurora-file-placement: no capacity term was read"

# invariant: the module unit still overflows at sixteen nodes, which is the finding this witness
# inherits and the whole reason a file unit is under test.
assert scan.out contains "module_unit_overflows_sixteen=yes" else "aurora-file-placement: modules began to fit -- the forced coarsening is no longer forced"

# invariant: the file unit fits where the module unit does not, so the erratum's named step is
# available rather than merely proposed.
assert scan.out contains "unit_fits_sixteen=yes" else "aurora-file-placement: the largest file outgrew a node's share at sixteen -- read the scan, then the paper"

# invariant: and the file unit has its own ceiling one grid up. A reading that never refuses is a
# reading that cannot tell a fit from a tree it failed to open.
assert scan.out contains "unit_ceiling_nodes=16" else "aurora-file-placement: the file unit's ceiling moved -- read fit lines, then raise this"
assert scan.out contains "first_overflowing_nodes=64" else "aurora-file-placement: the grid where the file unit overflows moved"
assert scan.out contains "fit k=8 nodes=64" else "aurora-file-placement: the 64-node grid went ungraded"

# --- READING 2 -- what the finer graph holds ---------------------------------
# invariant: the file graph was resolved through symlinks and carries edges. Zig refuses an import
# escaping the root file's directory, so a cross-room dependency arrives only as a symlinked name.
assert scan.out contains "import_edges=" else "aurora-file-placement: no import graph was read"
assert scan.out contains "cross_room_edges=" else "aurora-file-placement: symlinked cross-room imports went unresolved"
assert scan.out contains "intra_room_edge_share=" else "aurora-file-placement: the room-invisible share went unread"
assert scan.out contains "edges_per_room_pair=" else "aurora-file-placement: the finer graph was never compared with the room graph"

# --- READING 3 -- the placement ----------------------------------------------
assert scan.out contains "reading3=read" else "aurora-file-placement: the placement reading reached no verdict"

# invariant: the capacity rule actually bound the packer -- a file it could not seat is counted
# rather than quietly dropped on node zero and forgotten.
assert scan.out contains "sixteen_infeasible_files=0" else "aurora-file-placement: a file could not be seated under the capacity rule"

# invariant: the layout is compared against a COUNT-MATCHED baseline as well as a free one. A node
# holding many files pays nothing for the traffic inside it, so a layout free to pile files up beats
# a spread baseline under any weights at all -- occupancy wearing the clothes of coupling.
assert scan.out contains "matched_gain_share=" else "aurora-file-placement: the count-matched baseline went unread"
assert scan.out contains "sixteen_beats_matched_floor=yes" else "aurora-file-placement: the layout stopped beating its own occupancy dealt at random -- the graph is buying nothing"

# invariant: the price of the forbidden coarsening is printed as two shares beside each other, so a
# reader sees what a module placement would have had free and what the file placement keeps.
assert scan.out contains "room_layout_same_node_share=" else "aurora-file-placement: the room layout's free traffic went unread"
assert scan.out contains "file_layout_same_node_share=" else "aurora-file-placement: the file layout's kept traffic went unread"
assert scan.out contains "free_traffic_lost=" else "aurora-file-placement: the price of the forced unit went unread"

# --- The control: real repositories in a throwaway pen -----------------------
say "aurora-file-placement: the control -- three real repositories in a throwaway pen..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/a/aurora_file_placement_control.sh"]
say ctl.out
assert ctl.ok else "aurora-file-placement: the control refused -- read its own leg lines"
assert ctl.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "aurora-file-placement: the control reached no ok verdict"

# invariant: the control tallies its own legs and this witness asserts both the count and the
# failure count, so a leg written tomorrow is heard the day it lands rather than passing unread
# under a green verdict.
assert ctl.out contains "control_failures=0" else "aurora-file-placement: a planted behavior differed from what was stated"
assert ctl.out contains "control_checks=64" else "aurora-file-placement: the control's leg count moved -- read it, then raise this line"

# invariant: each of the five mutations was planted AND bit. A refusal proven only in the passing
# direction cannot be told from a bypass.
assert ctl.out contains "leg m1_bites ok" else "aurora-file-placement: leaving import symlinks unresolved went unfelt"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m2_bites ok" else "aurora-file-placement: dropping the self-import guard went unfelt"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m3_bites ok" else "aurora-file-placement: pricing a mutual import twice went unfelt"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m4_bites ok" else "aurora-file-placement: the room comparison stopped separating intra from cross"
assert ctl.out contains "leg m5_bites ok" else "aurora-file-placement: removing the capacity test let a node fill past its bound"

# invariant: the refusing side of the capacity reading is proven on a pen holding one file too big
# for any node's share, so `file_fits=yes` on this tree is a reading rather than a constant.
assert ctl.out contains "leg p1_fit_k2_no ok" else "aurora-file-placement: an oversized file was read as fitting"
assert ctl.out contains "leg p1_fits_sixteen_no ok" else "aurora-file-placement: the pen's oversized file fit a sixteenth"
assert ctl.out contains "leg p1_ceiling_zero ok" else "aurora-file-placement: a tree with no fitting grid reported one"

# invariant: every way an edge list goes wrong is planted in one pen and each is refused by name --
# a self-import, an import naming no file, a mutual pair, and a cross-room import through a symlink.
assert ctl.out contains "leg p1_edges ok" else "aurora-file-placement: the pen's edge count moved -- a broken edge was admitted or a real one dropped"
assert ctl.out contains "leg p1_intra_share ok" else "aurora-file-placement: the pen's intra-room share moved"

# invariant: a tree with no Rye at all refuses rather than reading zero, since an empty population
# fits every node trivially and would score a perfect capacity reading.
assert ctl.out contains "leg p3_empty_verdict ok" else "aurora-file-placement: an empty tree was read as a real population"

say "GREEN: aurora-file-placement -- the file unit fits at sixteen nodes and overflows at sixty-four, its graph is mostly edges a room graph cannot see, and the layout beats its own occupancy dealt at random."
